<back><div type="verses">
<lg label="2."><l>Thy Word is like a starry host:</l><l>A thousand rays of light</l><l>Are seen to guide the traveler,</l><l>And make his pathway bright.</l><l>Thy Word is like an armory,</l><l>Where soldiers may repair,</l><l>And find, for life’s long battle day,</l><l>All needful weapons there.</l></lg>
<lg label="3."><l>O may I love Thy precious Word,</l><l>May I explore the mine,</l><l>May I its glorious riches take,</l><l>May light upon me shine.</l><l>O may I find my armor there,</l><l>Thy Word my trusty sword;</l><l>I’ll learn to fight with every foe</l><l>The battle of the Lord.</l></lg>
<lg label="4."><l>Word of the ever living God,</l><l>Will of His glorious Son;</l><l>Without Thee how could earth be trod,</l><l>Or God and Christ be won?</l><l>Lord, grant us all aright to learn</l><l>The wisdom it imparts,</l><l>And to its heav’nly teaching turn,</l><l>With simple, child-like hearts.</l></lg>
</div>
</back>
</music></mei>
